# A vim-shaped startup: enter the alternate screen, reserve a status row with
# DECSTBM, draw a tilde column and a status line, then leave. On exit the
# primary screen and its shell prompt must be intact.
size: 20x6
description: an editor's alternate-screen session leaves the primary screen intact

--- input
$\x20ls\r\nfile.txt\r\n$\x20vim\e[?1049h\e[1;1H\e[2J\e[1;20r
\e[1;1H~\e[2;1H~\e[3;1H~
\e[6;1H\e[7m-- INSERT --\e[0m
\e[?1049l

--- expect-grid
|$ ls|
|file.txt|
|$ vim|
||
||
||

--- expect-cursor
row=2 col=5
